1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:04,896
Inflation has crossed the Reserve Bank's
red line,

2
00:00:05,127 --> 00:00:12,594
a fresh push for women's reservation has
reopened the north–south debate,

3
00:00:12,907 --> 00:00:18,550
Delhi breathed air about 17 times the safe
limit on Deepavali,

4
00:00:19,026 --> 00:00:23,696
and India's exports have hit an all-time
high.

5
00:00:23,865 --> 00:00:25,377
This week is very important!

6
00:00:25,925 --> 00:00:26,551
I am Mounika,

7
00:00:26,591 --> 00:00:32,091
and today we decode the 13 strongest
stories of November's second week,

8
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:37,022
with real data, clear diagrams and one
practice question after every topic,

9
00:00:37,221 --> 00:00:40,753
plus a quick round of persons and places
in news.

10
00:00:40,799 --> 00:00:42,454
Let's start our journey.

11
00:00:42,744 --> 00:00:47,230
Here is our map: five stories on the
economy, four on polity and society,

12
00:00:47,499 --> 00:00:53,870
four on environment, health and the world,
and then persons and places in news.

13
00:00:53,910 --> 00:00:59,141
Story one: why has inflation crossed the
Reserve Bank's red line?

14
00:00:59,243 --> 00:01:07,573
Retail inflation in October rose to 6.09%,
up from 5.54 in September,

15
00:01:07,933 --> 00:01:09,843
according to the Ministry of Statistics.

16
00:01:10,553 --> 00:01:16,403
Food inflation jumped from 7.74 to 8.94%,

17
00:01:16,443 --> 00:01:22,493
and onion prices alone rose by about 116%
in a year.

18
00:01:22,654 --> 00:01:25,544
Now the framework. Since 2016,

19
00:01:25,814 --> 00:01:31,714
the Reserve Bank Act sets a target of 4%
consumer inflation,

20
00:01:31,834 --> 00:01:34,974
with a band of 2% on either side,

21
00:01:35,024 --> 00:01:38,244
so 6% is the upper limit.

22
00:01:38,324 --> 00:01:44,034
The six-member Monetary Policy Committee
sets the repo rate to keep inflation

23
00:01:44,174 --> 00:01:50,704
inside this band. And if average inflation
stays outside the band for three quarters

24
00:01:50,744 --> 00:01:56,084
in a row, the Reserve Bank must report to
the government, explaining why,

25
00:01:56,124 --> 00:01:58,186
and what it will do.

26
00:01:58,226 --> 00:02:00,516
So what does this mean?

27
00:02:00,716 --> 00:02:06,236
When food prices drive inflation, a rate
hike cannot grow more onions,

28
00:02:06,546 --> 00:02:11,806
so the quicker tools are on the supply
side: buffer stocks,

29
00:02:12,016 --> 00:02:13,696
imports and better storage.

30
00:02:13,906 --> 00:02:18,346
But if high food prices spread into wages
and other goods,

31
00:02:18,756 --> 00:02:21,106
the Committee may have to act.

32
00:02:21,146 --> 00:02:26,526
And notice: this October number comes from
the new consumer price series,

33
00:02:26,676 --> 00:02:29,146
with base year 2024.

34
00:02:29,974 --> 00:02:35,719
Prelims trap: consumer price data is
released by the National Statistics Office

35
00:02:35,759 --> 00:02:40,152
in the Ministry of Statistics, not by the
Reserve Bank;

36
00:02:40,431 --> 00:02:45,381
and the inflation target is set by the
government in consultation with the

37
00:02:45,421 --> 00:02:49,708
Reserve Bank, not by the Monetary Policy
Committee alone.

38
00:02:49,765 --> 00:02:50,765
Remember this.

39
00:02:51,674 --> 00:02:56,668
Your first question of the day: how many
of these three statements are correct?

40
00:03:03,279 --> 00:03:05,921
The answer is B, only two.

41
00:03:05,961 --> 00:03:11,903
The Reserve Bank does not release consumer
price data; the Statistics Ministry does.

42
00:03:11,943 --> 00:03:23,928
Story two: women's reservation was passed
in 2023, so why is it still not in force?

43
00:03:24,438 --> 00:03:31,111
The 106th Amendment of 2023 reserves
one-third of seats in the Lok Sabha and

44
00:03:31,151 --> 00:03:33,531
state assemblies for women.

45
00:03:33,712 --> 00:03:42,875
But Article 334A says it will start only
after a delimitation based on the first

46
00:03:42,915 --> 00:03:45,566
census taken after that law,

47
00:03:45,836 --> 00:03:48,607
and the reservation then lasts 15 years.

48
00:03:48,847 --> 00:03:52,515
So the chain is: census, then
delimitation, then reservation.

49
00:03:52,555 --> 00:03:54,327
In April this year,

50
00:03:54,367 --> 00:04:02,205
the government tried to speed this up with
the Constitution 131st Amendment Bill,

51
00:04:02,245 --> 00:04:09,358
which would also expand the Lok Sabha from
543 seats to as many as 850.

52
00:04:09,398 --> 00:04:13,742
It failed in the Lok Sabha, 298 votes to
230,

53
00:04:13,782 --> 00:04:15,956
short of the two-thirds it needed.

54
00:04:16,063 --> 00:04:22,352
Now the government is reported to be
planning a special session to try again.

55
00:04:22,431 --> 00:04:25,508
Why the fight? Seats are shared by
population.

56
00:04:26,208 --> 00:04:30,075
States that controlled their population,
mostly in the south,

57
00:04:30,423 --> 00:04:35,471
fear losing their share of seats, while
faster-growing states,

58
00:04:35,511 --> 00:04:38,078
mostly in the north, would gain.

59
00:04:38,279 --> 00:04:46,366
That is why the 84th Amendment of 2001
froze the seat shares until the first

60
00:04:46,406 --> 00:04:48,640
census after 2026.

61
00:04:48,758 --> 00:04:54,645
So, this is not just women's reservation;
it is about federal balance.

62
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:58,906
Prelims trap: a constitutional amendment
needs a special majority:

63
00:04:58,946 --> 00:05:02,168
a majority of the total membership of the
House,

64
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:05,202
and two-thirds of those present and
voting.

65
00:05:05,242 --> 00:05:12,037
That is why the April bill failed, even
with more votes for it than against.

66
00:05:12,108 --> 00:05:14,735
Now a Statement-one, Statement-two
question.

67
00:05:14,775 --> 00:05:17,753
Decide whether the second explains the
first.

68
00:05:24,325 --> 00:05:26,355
The answer is A.

69
00:05:26,395 --> 00:05:27,581
Both are correct,

70
00:05:27,809 --> 00:05:34,132
and the special majority rule explains why
more votes for the bill were still not

71
00:05:34,172 --> 00:05:35,172
enough.

72
00:05:35,676 --> 00:05:41,747
Story three: what did Delhi really breathe
on Deepavali night?

73
00:05:41,924 --> 00:05:46,064
According to the Centre for Research on
Energy and Clean Air,

74
00:05:46,127 --> 00:05:52,220
Delhi's average fine dust, PM 2.5, on
Deepavali, November eighth,

75
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:56,964
was 257 micrograms per cubic metre:

76
00:05:57,154 --> 00:06:01,994
more than four times India's own daily
standard of 60,

77
00:06:02,524 --> 00:06:08,254
and about 17 times the World Health
Organization's guideline of 15.

78
00:06:08,404 --> 00:06:15,010
That night, 20 of Delhi's 59 stations were
in the severe category,

79
00:06:15,050 --> 00:06:21,690
and at the worst hour, 36 monitoring
stations were not reporting data at all.

80
00:06:21,730 --> 00:06:26,105
Delhi's emergency plan, the Graded
Response Action Plan,

81
00:06:26,145 --> 00:06:31,879
works like a ladder: stage 1 when the Air
Quality Index is poor, 201 to 300;

82
00:06:31,919 --> 00:06:39,970
stage 2 when it is very poor, 301 to 400;
stage 3 when it is severe, 401 to 450;

83
00:06:40,010 --> 00:06:46,377
and stage 4, severe plus, above 450, which
can stop construction and most trucks.

84
00:06:46,597 --> 00:06:48,838
But crackers are only the spark.

85
00:06:48,993 --> 00:06:52,431
Winter brings calm winds and a temperature
inversion,

86
00:06:52,818 --> 00:06:56,579
which works like a lid and traps smoke
near the ground;

87
00:06:57,177 --> 00:07:01,360
stubble fires in Punjab and Haryana add to
it;

88
00:07:01,455 --> 00:07:04,108
and vehicles and dust are always there.

89
00:07:04,193 --> 00:07:06,474
So even with green crackers,

90
00:07:06,790 --> 00:07:12,116
one night can push a city that is already
choking into the severe zone.

91
00:07:12,156 --> 00:07:18,067
Prelims trap: the Graded Response Action
Plan is enforced by the Commission for Air

92
00:07:18,107 --> 00:07:23,874
Quality Management, a statutory body set
up by a 2021 Act,

93
00:07:23,947 --> 00:07:26,520
not by the Central Pollution Control
Board.

94
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,560
Remember this.

95
00:07:27,859 --> 00:07:34,279
Pause and answer: how many of these three
statements are correct?

96
00:07:35,986 --> 00:07:39,425
The answer is C, all three.

97
00:07:39,465 --> 00:07:49,089
Severe is 401 to 450, India's daily
standard is 60,

98
00:07:49,132 --> 00:07:52,330
and the Commission enforces the plan.

99
00:07:52,546 --> 00:07:53,562
Three big stories done,

100
00:07:53,602 --> 00:07:56,998
10 to go. If you have stayed till here,

101
00:07:57,038 --> 00:08:01,973
you are a serious aspirant! Now let us go from
the air we breathe to the health of our

102
00:08:02,013 --> 00:08:03,013
people.

103
00:08:03,203 --> 00:08:06,963
Story four: India has a quarter of the
world's tuberculosis.

104
00:08:07,563 --> 00:08:08,563
Is that changing?

105
00:08:08,907 --> 00:08:15,229
The World Health Organization's Global
Tuberculosis Report 2026 says India still

106
00:08:15,269 --> 00:08:19,747
accounts for about one in four TB cases in
the world,

107
00:08:19,787 --> 00:08:23,117
and about 23% of TB deaths.

108
00:08:23,157 --> 00:08:29,047
But India's TB death rate has fallen 38%
since 2015,

109
00:08:29,220 --> 00:08:33,968
from about 280 to 180 deaths per million
people,

110
00:08:34,008 --> 00:08:39,091
a little faster than the global fall of
35%.

111
00:08:39,131 --> 00:08:45,138
Worldwide, about 10.6 million people fell
ill with TB in 2025,

112
00:08:45,178 --> 00:08:47,889
and 1.13 million died.

113
00:08:48,073 --> 00:08:49,179
And notice this:

114
00:08:49,219 --> 00:08:54,014
the World Health Organization has not
published India's new incidence estimates

115
00:08:54,064 --> 00:08:57,453
this year, because they are being
reviewed.

116
00:08:58,088 --> 00:08:59,831
Why is TB so stubborn?

117
00:09:00,362 --> 00:09:05,302
It spreads through the air in crowded
homes, it feeds on undernutrition,

118
00:09:05,693 --> 00:09:09,670
and drug-resistant TB needs long, costly
treatment;

119
00:09:10,123 --> 00:09:15,362
India is among four countries with over
half the world's multidrug-resistant

120
00:09:16,465 --> 00:09:23,671
cases. That is why nutrition support under
the Nikshay Poshan Yojana matters as much

121
00:09:23,711 --> 00:09:24,711
as medicines.

122
00:09:24,859 --> 00:09:29,539
Prelims trap: the global goal to end TB is
2030,

123
00:09:29,932 --> 00:09:32,161
under the Sustainable Development Goals,

124
00:09:32,201 --> 00:09:41,094
but India had set itself an earlier target
of 2025, which it has missed.

125
00:09:41,178 --> 00:09:44,889
Which one of these statements about TB is
correct?

126
00:09:51,510 --> 00:09:53,075
The answer is B:

127
00:09:53,269 --> 00:09:57,325
India accounts for about a quarter of the
world's TB cases.

128
00:09:57,620 --> 00:10:02,139
Remember, the 38% fall is in deaths, not
in cases.

129
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:08,477
Story five: India just had its best month
ever for exports.

130
00:10:09,121 --> 00:10:10,965
What does it really mean?

131
00:10:11,222 --> 00:10:17,162
In October, merchandise exports touched a
record 49.47 billion dollars,

132
00:10:17,202 --> 00:10:21,361
up about 45% from a year ago.

133
00:10:21,401 --> 00:10:29,812
Engineering goods rose 36%, electronics
63%, and petroleum products 140%.

134
00:10:29,852 --> 00:10:33,297
But goods imports were 89.35 billion
dollars,

135
00:10:33,337 --> 00:10:36,852
so the goods trade deficit was about 40
billion.

136
00:10:37,093 --> 00:10:43,182
Services saved the day: services exports
of about 40.5 billion dollars,

137
00:10:43,433 --> 00:10:50,163
against imports of about 20.7, brought the
overall deficit down to about 20 billion.

138
00:10:50,371 --> 00:10:55,937
So India still buys more goods than it
sells, mainly crude oil,

139
00:10:55,977 --> 00:10:57,446
electronics and gold,

140
00:10:57,486 --> 00:11:02,770
but earns a big surplus from services like
software and business services.

141
00:11:04,077 --> 00:11:11,205
And watch petroleum: India imports crude,
refines it and exports the products,

142
00:11:11,486 --> 00:11:17,251
so oil prices move both our imports and
our exports.

143
00:11:17,687 --> 00:11:21,840
Prelims trap: the trade balance covers
only goods and services;

144
00:11:22,194 --> 00:11:27,190
the current account also adds remittances
and income flows,

145
00:11:27,286 --> 00:11:29,477
and India is the world's largest receiver
of remittances.

146
00:11:29,517 --> 00:11:36,208
Four statements on trade.

147
00:11:36,248 --> 00:11:39,454
How many of them are correct?

148
00:11:44,265 --> 00:11:48,980
The answer is C, only three.

149
00:11:49,202 --> 00:11:58,429
India ran a goods trade deficit in
October, not a surplus.

150
00:11:59,731 --> 00:12:03,561
Story six: half a billion Indians out of
poverty, but measured by which line?

151
00:12:03,601 --> 00:12:08,831
The World Bank's October brief says
extreme poverty in India,

152
00:12:09,551 --> 00:12:17,031
at 3 dollars a day, fell from 27.1% in
2011 to 2.6% in 2023;

153
00:12:17,441 --> 00:12:19,961
at the higher line of 4 dollars 20,

154
00:12:20,191 --> 00:12:24,231
it fell from 57.7 to 16.1%.

155
00:12:24,851 --> 00:12:31,541
Remember, the World Bank raised its
international poverty line to 3 dollars a

156
00:12:31,581 --> 00:12:43,904
day in 2025, and critics say part of the
fall reflects new data and methods.

157
00:12:43,944 --> 00:12:45,670
Quick one: who publishes the global
Multidimensional Poverty Index?

158
00:12:52,820 --> 00:12:59,130
The answer is B: the United Nations
Development Programme with Oxford;

159
00:12:59,468 --> 00:13:03,759
in India, NITI Aayog publishes the
national index,

160
00:13:04,039 --> 00:13:08,022
and the World Bank measures income and
spending.

161
00:13:08,293 --> 00:13:17,293
Story seven: three Cabinet decisions for
small entrepreneurs and farmers.

162
00:13:17,699 --> 00:13:20,356
Stand-Up India, launched in 2016,

163
00:13:20,396 --> 00:13:25,415
gives loans of 10 lakh to 1 crore rupees
to Scheduled Caste,

164
00:13:25,455 --> 00:13:28,998
Scheduled Tribe and women entrepreneurs
for new enterprises,

165
00:13:29,038 --> 00:13:31,854
and now runs till March 2031.

166
00:13:32,007 --> 00:13:37,445
The Credit Guarantee Fund for Micro Units,
which backs small Mudra loans,

167
00:13:37,485 --> 00:13:39,707
also runs till 2031,

168
00:13:39,917 --> 00:13:43,542
with a corpus of 5,000 crore rupees.

169
00:13:43,582 --> 00:13:44,771
For the rabi season,

170
00:13:44,811 --> 00:13:51,711
the Cabinet approved about 62,370 crore
rupees of nutrient-based subsidy for

171
00:13:51,751 --> 00:13:53,629
phosphatic and potassic fertilisers,

172
00:13:53,669 --> 00:14:03,104
and it also cleared about 3,230 crore
rupees for the Yuge Yugeen Bharat Museum

173
00:14:03,144 --> 00:14:06,357
in the old North and South Block.

174
00:14:06,397 --> 00:14:11,626
Prelims trap: urea is not covered by the
nutrient-based subsidy;

175
00:14:11,666 --> 00:14:14,500
it has its own controlled price.

176
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:19,058
The nutrient-based system, in place since
2010,

177
00:14:19,112 --> 00:14:25,151
covers phosphatic and potassic fertilisers
like D A P.

178
00:14:25,491 --> 00:14:29,693
How many of these three statements are
correct?

179
00:14:36,413 --> 00:14:39,962
The answer is B, only two.

180
00:14:40,072 --> 00:14:44,131
Urea is outside the nutrient-based
subsidy.

181
00:14:45,063 --> 00:14:49,563
Story eight: why did India ban the export
of battery black mass?

182
00:14:49,816 --> 00:14:52,620
When old lithium-ion batteries are
shredded,

183
00:14:53,012 --> 00:14:57,529
they leave a dark powder called black
mass, rich in lithium, nickel,

184
00:14:57,569 --> 00:14:59,772
cobalt, manganese and graphite.

185
00:15:00,083 --> 00:15:01,284
On November 11th,

186
00:15:01,586 --> 00:15:06,474
the Directorate General of Foreign Trade
moved it from free to prohibited for

187
00:15:06,514 --> 00:15:12,482
export, under the Foreign Trade
Development and Regulation Act of 1992.

188
00:15:12,667 --> 00:15:15,445
Why? Remember last week's story:

189
00:15:15,485 --> 00:15:20,221
2,814 crore rupees for processing lithium
and nickel,

190
00:15:20,261 --> 00:15:24,095
and a 1,500 crore rupee recycling scheme.

191
00:15:24,281 --> 00:15:27,469
Keeping black mass at home feeds those
plants,

192
00:15:27,517 --> 00:15:35,206
because recycling is a mine above the
ground for a country with few lithium

193
00:15:35,246 --> 00:15:35,702
reserves.

194
00:15:35,742 --> 00:15:40,058
The Directorate General of Foreign Trade
works under which ministry?

195
00:15:46,786 --> 00:15:51,109
The answer is B, the Ministry of Commerce
and Industry.

196
00:15:51,818 --> 00:16:00,289
Story nine: is the world ready for the
warming that is already coming?

197
00:16:00,859 --> 00:16:06,043
The United Nations Environment Programme's
Adaptation Gap Report 2026,

198
00:16:06,599 --> 00:16:08,110
titled Ready? Not.,

199
00:16:08,150 --> 00:16:14,921
says developing countries will need about
305 billion dollars a year for adaptation

200
00:16:15,071 --> 00:16:16,382
by 2035,

201
00:16:16,793 --> 00:16:24,372
but in 2024 they received only about 28 to
32 billion in public adaptation finance.

202
00:16:24,412 --> 00:16:30,652
Even tripling it would cover only 20 to
29% of the need.

203
00:16:30,692 --> 00:16:35,382
Simply put: mitigation means reducing,
adaptation means coping.

204
00:16:36,763 --> 00:16:39,237
Match the report with its publisher.

205
00:16:40,230 --> 00:16:41,723
How many pairs are

206
00:16:47,909 --> 00:16:47,885
correct?

207
00:16:47,925 --> 00:16:52,855
The answer is C, all three.

208
00:16:53,186 --> 00:16:56,913
Nine done! Now let's turn to our rivers, rights and
the world.

209
00:16:56,953 --> 00:17:02,992
Story 10: why are the Adi people of
Arunachal Pradesh protesting a dam on the

210
00:17:03,032 --> 00:17:03,898
Siang?

211
00:17:03,938 --> 00:17:09,141
One river, many names: it rises in Tibet
as the Yarlung Tsangpo,

212
00:17:09,412 --> 00:17:14,866
enters Arunachal Pradesh as the Siang,
becomes the Brahmaputra in Assam,

213
00:17:15,206 --> 00:17:17,587
and is called the Jamuna in Bangladesh.

214
00:17:18,172 --> 00:17:24,031
The Siang Upper Multipurpose Project,
planned at around 11,000 megawatts,

215
00:17:24,363 --> 00:17:27,577
is meant to store water and act as a
buffer,

216
00:17:27,999 --> 00:17:33,769
especially because China has begun a giant
hydropower project upstream on the Yarlung

217
00:17:33,809 --> 00:17:39,207
Tsangpo. But the Adi community fears that
dozens of villages could be submerged,

218
00:17:39,679 --> 00:17:41,261
and the protests continue.

219
00:17:42,731 --> 00:17:44,820
Match the river's name with the region.

220
00:17:45,030 --> 00:17:46,730
How many pairs are correct?

221
00:17:53,281 --> 00:17:55,934
The answer is B, only two.

222
00:17:55,974 --> 00:17:59,640
The Jamuna is the name in Bangladesh, not
in Assam.

223
00:18:00,829 --> 00:18:05,745
Story 11: can Karnataka save its higher
quota through the Ninth Schedule?

224
00:18:06,207 --> 00:18:14,717
In 2022 Karnataka raised Scheduled Caste
reservation from 15 to 17% and Scheduled

225
00:18:14,777 --> 00:18:18,217
Tribe reservation from three to 7%,

226
00:18:18,257 --> 00:18:21,297
taking total reservation to 56%.

227
00:18:21,397 --> 00:18:26,207
In October, the High Court struck down the
hike for breaching the 50% ceiling,

228
00:18:26,567 --> 00:18:30,004
and the state now wants the law placed in
the Ninth Schedule.

229
00:18:30,044 --> 00:18:36,698
The Ninth Schedule was added by the First
Amendment in 1951, with Article 31B,

230
00:18:36,738 --> 00:18:39,781
to protect land reform laws from court
challenges.

231
00:18:39,821 --> 00:18:44,642
The Indra Sawhney judgment of 1992 set the
50% ceiling,

232
00:18:44,682 --> 00:18:50,104
and Tamil Nadu's 69% reservation went into
the Ninth Schedule through the 76th

233
00:18:51,061 --> 00:18:52,612
Amendment of 1994.

234
00:18:52,922 --> 00:18:56,667
But in I R Coelho, in 2007,

235
00:18:56,745 --> 00:19:02,159
the Supreme Court held that laws added
after April 24th, 1973,

236
00:19:03,037 --> 00:19:06,950
can still be tested against the basic
structure.

237
00:19:07,033 --> 00:19:11,101
Prelims trap: only Parliament, through a
constitutional amendment,

238
00:19:11,141 --> 00:19:13,539
can add a law to the Ninth Schedule;

239
00:19:13,579 --> 00:19:15,753
a state legislature cannot.

240
00:19:15,793 --> 00:19:16,793
Remember this.

241
00:19:17,656 --> 00:19:20,770
How many of these three statements are
correct?

242
00:19:27,392 --> 00:19:29,823
The answer is A, only one.

243
00:19:29,863 --> 00:19:32,985
The Ninth Schedule came with the First
Amendment;

244
00:19:33,238 --> 00:19:38,711
but its laws are not fully immune, and a
state cannot add them.

245
00:19:39,087 --> 00:19:45,407
Story 12, from the sea: IMNEX 26.

246
00:19:45,897 --> 00:19:50,468
The eighth India–Myanmar Naval Exercise,
IMNEX 26,

247
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:54,606
was held at Visakhapatnam from November
10th to 14th,

248
00:19:54,805 --> 00:19:58,420
with the Indian Naval Ships Rana and
Sumedha.

249
00:19:58,460 --> 00:20:04,409
Now the trap table: SLINEX is the navy
exercise with Sri Lanka,

250
00:20:04,449 --> 00:20:08,400
Mitra Shakti is the army exercise with Sri
Lanka,

251
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:13,457
and Malabar brings together India, the
United States, Japan and Australia.

252
00:20:13,497 --> 00:20:17,169
Four exercise pairs. How many are
correctly matched?

253
00:20:23,780 --> 00:20:26,914
The answer is D, all four.

254
00:20:26,954 --> 00:20:33,767
And story 13: today, November 14th, is
Children's Day.

255
00:20:33,849 --> 00:20:38,177
India marks Children's Day on November
14th, Jawaharlal Nehru's birthday,

256
00:20:38,217 --> 00:20:43,651
while the United Nations' Universal
Children's Day is November 20th.

257
00:20:43,691 --> 00:20:45,775
And on November 11th,

258
00:20:45,815 --> 00:20:51,746
we marked National Education Day for
Maulana Abul Kalam Azad,

259
00:20:51,786 --> 00:20:53,919
our first Education Minister,

260
00:20:53,959 --> 00:21:01,533
while the United Nations' International
Day of Education is January 24th.

261
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:07,059
Last question of the day: how many of
these three statements are correct?

262
00:21:12,685 --> 00:21:15,567
The answer is B, only two.

263
00:21:15,607 --> 00:21:21,295
National Education Day is for Maulana
Azad, not Doctor Radhakrishnan.

264
00:21:21,929 --> 00:21:30,153
Before we finish, a quick Prelims round:
persons, places and awards in news.

265
00:21:30,193 --> 00:21:36,618
First, persons. Anuj Shrivatri of Madhya
Pradesh became India's 100th chess

266
00:21:36,893 --> 00:21:42,220
Grandmaster on November eighth, the first
from his state; remember,

267
00:21:42,715 --> 00:21:45,858
India's first Grandmaster was Viswanathan
Anand,

268
00:21:45,898 --> 00:21:54,477
in 1988. British writer M John Harrison
won the Booker Prize 2026 for The End of

269
00:21:54,517 --> 00:21:58,127
Everything, and is reported to be its
oldest winner.

270
00:21:58,167 --> 00:22:02,746
And at the National Sports Awards on
November 13th,

271
00:22:02,786 --> 00:22:07,364
17 athletes received the Arjuna Award,
including Tejaswin Shankar,

272
00:22:07,404 --> 00:22:10,059
Divya Deshmukh and Vidit Gujrathi,

273
00:22:10,228 --> 00:22:14,644
but no one was selected for the Khel Ratna
this year.

274
00:22:15,138 --> 00:22:18,968
Now places. Antalya, on Türkiye's
Mediterranean coast,

275
00:22:19,008 --> 00:22:25,495
is hosting the climate summit COP 31, from
November ninth to 20th,

276
00:22:25,535 --> 00:22:28,357
with Australia leading the negotiations.

277
00:22:28,415 --> 00:22:34,082
Manila in the Philippines hosts the ASEAN
and East Asia Summits next week;

278
00:22:34,122 --> 00:22:36,296
India is a member of the East Asia Summit,

279
00:22:36,336 --> 00:22:37,482
but not of ASEAN.

280
00:22:37,522 --> 00:22:40,984
Shenzhen in China hosts the APEC leaders,
and remember,

281
00:22:41,024 --> 00:22:43,318
India is not an APEC member.

282
00:22:43,358 --> 00:22:46,819
And Mekedatu in Karnataka is back in the
news:

283
00:22:46,859 --> 00:22:54,863
Karnataka wants clearance for a 16,745
crore rupee balancing reservoir on the

284
00:22:54,903 --> 00:23:01,170
Cauvery, inside the Cauvery Wildlife
Sanctuary, while Tamil Nadu opposes it.

285
00:23:01,210 --> 00:23:02,694
Four pairs from this round.

286
00:23:02,734 --> 00:23:04,998
How many are correctly matched?

287
00:23:11,726 --> 00:23:15,986
The answer is C, only three.

288
00:23:16,225 --> 00:23:20,578
Mekedatu is on the Cauvery, not the
Krishna.

289
00:23:21,428 --> 00:23:26,747
And for Mains, here is this week's one
writing question:

290
00:23:27,573 --> 00:23:33,803
should Lok Sabha seat shares stay frozen
to protect states that controlled their

291
00:23:33,843 --> 00:23:39,017
population? Discuss it with reference to
women's reservation and delimitation.

292
00:23:39,057 --> 00:23:41,301
Write 250 words,

293
00:23:41,341 --> 00:23:44,374
and write your answer in the comments.

294
00:23:44,414 --> 00:23:47,255
All 14 practice questions, with answers,

295
00:23:47,295 --> 00:23:50,070
are in the practice sheet linked in the
description.

296
00:23:50,590 --> 00:23:52,852
That was November's second week: 13
stories,

297
00:23:52,892 --> 00:23:55,623
with the data and the diagrams behind each
one.

298
00:23:55,764 --> 00:23:59,367
If this helped, share it with one friend
who is preparing with you,

299
00:23:59,407 --> 00:24:01,328
and subscribe for every Sunday's class.

300
00:24:01,368 --> 00:24:03,599
All the best, and see you next Sunday!

